course: dictionary
lesson: 15034
title: Resume: start again, or send your CV
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Resume» is a verb. It means to start again after a pause. «The lesson resumed after break» means the lesson began again at the point where it had stopped. The verb changes its ending: resumes, resumed, resuming.
explain: In formal English, «resume» can mean to take back a seat or place. «Please resume your seats» is a polite way of saying sit back down. You can check the meaning by swapping in «start again» or «sit back down» and seeing whether the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Résumé» is a different word with accents on the letters. In the USA and Canada, a résumé is a document listing your work and education when you apply for a job (in the UK, this is called a CV). A résumé can also be a short summary. The spelling is the clue: the accents tell you it is the noun.
fact: «Resume» means to start again after a pause.
fact: «Resume» can also mean to take back a seat or place, as in «resume your seats».
fact: «Résumé» is a noun with accents: a document listing your work and education for a job, or a short summary.
fact: In North America, a résumé is the document you send when you apply for a job; in the UK, it is called a CV.
fact: The verb changes its ending: resume, resumes, resumed, resuming.
exercise: «After the rain stopped, the football match will resume.» What does resume mean here? | *To start again after a pause | To run very fast | To cancel the match completely | To end for the day
exercise: «Please resume your seats.» What does resume mean here? | To sing loudly | To stand up and leave | *To sit back down | To buy new chairs
exercise: In North America, what is a résumé? | A cake for a birthday party | A type of sandwich | A short holiday trip | *A document listing your work and education when you apply for a job
test: The class will resume its reading after lunch. What does resume mean? | Read a book backwards | Stop reading forever | *Start again after a pause | Ask for a new book
test: Which spelling means the job document used in North America? | resuming | resumed | *résumé | resumes
exam: Jun says, «The show will resume at seven.» What does resume mean? | Finish for ever | *Start again after a stop | Move house | Be cancelled
